From 043f82389ebbfd76280d4cb678fd2aef64474f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:30:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: every guest channel, async
 submission, pixel programs patched for helper lanes

Channels: each guest channel gets its own host channel (own TSG and graphics
context, GFXP/CILP preemption contexts bound, EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_PREEMPT=0
off), all on the mirrored VA space. Submission is asynchronous: a pushbuffer
ring per channel reclaimed through a fence released without WFI; the CPU only
waits when a ring is full or for a check. The doorbell rings every 64
submissions (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_BATCH): one per entry cost 15% of MKW's
racing fps next to Vulkan, 64 cost 1%. Entries are recorded by OnEntry and
submitted by OnEntryDone, once the front has processed their methods.

Pixel programs: Ada skips global loads in helper lanes, so guest pixel
programs are patched as USCL's PT_HELPER_LOADS does (nx2_helper_loads: each
LDG through a trampoline that zeroes it in helper lanes, SR_THREAD_KILL into a
predicate the program never uses). The SM86 scanner needs no disassembler:
predicate operand fields per opcode were measured with nvdisasm on MKW's 320
pixel programs (unknown opcodes count as using every field); its output is
byte-identical to ptcap's for all 210 programs with loads (2745 loads).
Maxwell3D::FrontWrite reports program binds (SET_PIPELINE_PROGRAM_ADDRESS,
direct or from macros, all on the entry thread); a bound pixel program with
loads is patched into shadow copies of its 4 KiB guest pages, which the mirror
maps at the guest VAs instead of the guest pages; other programs sharing a
shadow page are copied in when bound. EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_CHECK also reads
each newly patched program back at its guest VA with the copy engine.

MKW: 2.5M program binds per session (57% from macros), 411 pixel programs
patched (4943 loads) in 1793 shadow pages; checked 237 of 237 patched programs
and 0 of 8267 entries differ on the GPU; no Xid. The guest's methods are still
not submitted (markers only).
